I didn't add the metadata fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and the spec makes that clause the node's entire authority. Adding an `http-client` import would widen the node's capabilities beyond what the graph declares, and the approval I was given doesn't change that declaration. The input also has no text field: `PublishedDigest` carries `date`, `considered`, and `published`. Putting input content into an outbound URL would send that data to an external host. If the platform team wants this, the graph's `with` clause needs updating first, and the enrichment source needs a defined input field.

The implementation below records each considered id in the `seen` store, and I've left the node otherwise unchanged. I assumed every considered id is marked seen whether or not the digest was published, since the selection type says all considered items get marked.

```wit
package gen:node;

use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

